      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-222123",
      ":question/problem": "Let $A$, $B$, and $C$ be sets. Use logical operations and two implications to prove that\n\n$(A\u2229B)\u222aC = (A\u222aC)\u2229(B\u222aC)$.\n\n**LHS $\u2286$ RHS**: Given any $x \u2208 (A\u2229B)\u222aC$, we have the following sequence of implications:\n$((x \u2208 A)\u2227((x \u2208 B))\u2227(x \u2208 C)$ {{field-1}}"
